 "lines": [
  {
   "id": "o01",
   "at": 0.6,
   "text": "Every contract makes promises."
  },
  {
   "id": "o02",
   "at": 3.0,
   "text": "Delivery in six weeks. Discounts at volume. Rebates. Payment terms."
  },
  {
   "id": "o03",
   "at": 9.6,
   "text": "But checking them is manual, and limited to a few contracts. When a promise is broken, the claim is often never made."
  },
  {
   "id": "o04",
   "at": 17.9,
   "text": "Meet Obligation Management.",
   "caption": false
  },
  {
   "id": "o05",
   "at": 21.8,
   "text": "It tracks contractual obligations across every purchase order, and calculates the claim when one is broken."
  },
  {
   "id": "o06",
   "at": 28.4,
   "text": "Start with the big picture: violations, potential claims, and the suppliers in breach."
  },
  {
   "id": "o07",
   "at": 34.6,
   "text": "Then drill down. From supplier, to contract,"
  },
  {
   "id": "o08",
   "at": 38.6,
   "text": "to purchase order, to each individual obligation."
  },
  {
   "id": "o09",
   "at": 42.3,
   "text": "Here's the clause, straight from Sirion Contract Watch. Lead time: six weeks."
  },
  {
   "id": "o10",
   "at": 48.6,
   "text": "And here's what happened. The goods took almost nine."
  },
  {
   "id": "o11",
   "at": 52.4,
   "text": "The AI checks the order against the clause, and flags the breach. Three weeks late."
  },
  {
   "id": "o12",
   "at": 58.5,
   "text": "Then it calculates the claim, step by step. Three weeks, at ten percent a week, of the order value. Checked against the cap. A claim of over one hundred and seven thousand pounds."
  },
  {
   "id": "o13",
   "at": 71.5,
   "text": "New obligation types take minutes to set up. Delivery, payment, quality, compliance. The AI writes the validation logic for each, and runs it across every order."
  },
  {
   "id": "o14",
   "at": 84.3,
   "text": "And when the data isn't the whole story, a buyer or category manager can override the result, with the justification on record."
  },
  {
   "id": "o15",
   "at": 92.8,
   "text": "Every obligation tracked. Every claim counted. No value left on the table."
  },
  {
   "id": "o16",
   "at": 100.8,
   "text": "Obligation Management. Promises, kept.",
   "caption": false
  }
 ]
}